PHASE IV: FAIL-SAFE WATCHDOG (FSW 2.0) AND BUS PRESSURE SENSING\uc0\u8232 The FSW 2.0 is the autonomous guardian of the Stratum, monitoring both thermal and electrical pressure.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. Bus Pressure and Liveness Sensing\
The FSW 2.0 monitors the "Pressure Stall Information" (PSI) and PCIe "Transaction Pending" bits. If the Core-Ghetto (Cores 0-1) becomes unresponsive due to an I/O storm, the FSW 2.0 executes an "Administrative Offload," suspending non-essential system slices to restore SSH and HID availability.\
B. Thermal Gradient Compensation (TGC)\
If the silicon temperature reaches T_crit - 5C, the FSW 2.0 executes a "Micro-Throttling Pulse."\
Logic: Instead of a global frequency drop, it inserts "Nop-Gaps" into the instruction stream of the Phantom Core for 10 microseconds. This lowers the Dynamic Power (P_dyn) just enough to vent heat without losing the "Performance" governor state or clearing the cache.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
PHASE V: PREDICTIVE SHADOW-SPINNING (PSS) AND MEMORY WARMING\uc0\u8232 APS eliminates the "Cold Start" penalty through surgical memory staging based on LBR telemetry.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. LBR-Intent Mapping\
By reading the Last Branch Record (LBR) registers, APS identifies the call-stack patterns that precede a mission-critical operation.\
Logic: It initiates a "Memory Warm-up" (pre-fetching and hugepage-locking) 2-5 milliseconds before the target application requires the data.\
Equation 3: Warm-Start Readiness (W_sr)\
W_sr = (T_predict - T_overhead) > 0\
This ensures that the first instruction of the compute pulse finds its data already residing in the L1/L2 hierarchy.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
