PHASE VI: ENTROPY-INJECTION PROTOCOL (EIP)\uc0\u8232 Heavy throttling of background processes can starve the system of randomness, causing cryptographic stalls.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A. RDRAND/RDSEED Direct Priming\
APS monitors /dev/random and proactively injects hardware-generated entropy into the kernel pool. This ensures that encrypted 5G/6G signals or secure HFT transactions never suffer from "Entropy Exhaustion" latency.\
